KG42.register("rules-afd3420531c200ee75317392",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R009","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"The local clearing optimization determines bilateral trading quantities and yields their P2P clearing prices; the energy-equilibrium constraint corresponds to the price multiplier. Scope: Individual bilateral P2P trades in the proposed local energy market. Condition: At the optimal solution of objective (39), using KKT conditions and the relaxation of constraints (36)-(38).","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E36"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Individual bilateral P2P trades in the proposed local energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E36"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit","symbol":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Individual bilateral P2P buying quantity/energy bid by prosumer j from prosumer i at time t, used in the LMO optimization (39) and bounded by the prosumer's total P2P buying bid and binary trading status in (36).","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative real in the clearing constraints; 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t} for j≠i and t∈T (Eq. 36). Fig. 12 reports traded amounts in kW.","unit":"kW","indices":["j∈J","i∈J, i≠j","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e003"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-Pps-ijt","symbol":"P^{ps}_{i,j,t}","meaning":"Individual bilateral P2P selling quantity by prosumer i to prosumer j at time t, with the subscript order used in Eqs. (38)-(39). The source uses P^{ps}_{j,i,t} in (37) and P^{ps}_{i,j,t} in (38)-(39); the exact cross-subscript identification is noted for revision.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonpositive real; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0 for (j,i)∈J with i≠j and t∈T (Eqs. 38-39). The matching bound in (37) is stated with P^{ps}_{j,i,t} in the supplied text.","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈J","j∈J, i≠j","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e002"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt","symbol":"\\lambda^{c}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"P2P trading price between prosumers j and i at time t, obtained as the price of the optimal solution of LMO optimization (39) using KKT conditions and identified in the source as the Lagrange multiplier corresponding to energy-equilibrium constraint (38).","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued price; the supplied text does not impose an explicit sign restriction on λ^c_{j,i,t}.","unit":"price unit as printed in Fig. 12 (¢); consistent with the \\Lambda price terms in (39)","indices":["j∈J","i∈J, i≠j","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt","symbol":"\\Lambda^{pb}_{j,t}","meaning":"Price for P2P trading in the buying term of objective (39), associated with prosumer j at time t; the source defines \\Lambda^{pb}_{j,t} and \\Lambda^{ps}_{i,t} as the prices for P2P trading between prosumer j and prosumer i at time t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price unit (¢ as printed in Fig. 12)","indices":["j∈J","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e004"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-ps-it","symbol":"\\Lambda^{ps}_{i,t}","meaning":"Price for P2P trading in the selling term of objective (39), associated with prosumer i at time t; the source defines \\Lambda^{pb}_{j,t} and \\Lambda^{ps}_{i,t} as the prices for P2P trading between prosumer j and prosumer i at time t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price unit (¢ as printed in Fig. 12)","indices":["i∈J","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e004"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-tau","symbol":"\\tau","meaning":"Time-slot duration/factor multiplying the double-sum objective in (39); the supplied source uses τ for trading intervals but does not state a general numerical value in this rule's evidence.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"time","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local clearing optimization determines bilateral trading quantities and yields their P2P clearing prices; the energy-equilibrium constraint corresponds to the price multiplier. Scope: Individual bilateral P2P trades in the proposed local energy market. Condition: At the optimal solution of objective (39), using KKT conditions and the relaxation of constraints (36)-(38).","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Formal transcription of the core local-clearing optimization in Eq. (39): the LMO minimizes, over individual bilateral P2P buying and selling quantities and the P2P trading price multiplier, the peer buying-cost and selling-revenue terms net of the multiplier-weighted equilibrium quantity, subject to (36)-(38).","expression":"\\min \\sum_{j\\in J}\\sum_{i\\in J\\,|\\,i\\ne j} \\left( \\left(P^{pb}_{j,i,t}\\Lambda^{pb}_{j,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}\\Lambda^{ps}_{i,t}\\right)-\\lambda^{c}_{j,i,t}\\left(P^{pb}_{j,i,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}\\right) \\right)\\tau;\\quad P^{ps}_{i,j,t}\\le 0,\\ \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\,|\\,j\\ne i,\\ \\forall t\\in T,\\quad \\text{subject to (36)-(38)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit","v141-c-R009-x-Pps-ijt","v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt","v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-ps-it","v141-c-R009-theta-tau"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Energy-equilibrium constraint (38): the P2P energy bought by prosumer j from prosumer i equals the negative of the P2P energy sold by prosumer i to prosumer j, with nonpositive selling quantities. The source explicitly states that this constraint corresponds to the Lagrange multiplier λ^c_{j,i,t} in (39).","expression":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}=0;\\quad P^{ps}_{i,j,t}\\le 0,\\quad \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\,|\\,i\\ne j,\\ \\forall t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit","v141-c-R009-x-Pps-ijt","v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e002","v141-b-g03-e004"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"Overview of the Proposed Framework","anchor_text":"unt Fig. 1. The proposed framework of DOE-based prosumers management in the LEM. ed ith consumption ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E36","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"energy by i to j. In (39), the third term presents the product of Lagrange multiplier λcj,i,t and th","equation_id":"(39)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The objective function (39) yields P2P trading bids (P^{pb}_{j,i,t} and P^{ps}_{i,j,t}) and a P2P trading price λ^{c}_{j,i,t} of the optimal solution using Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) conditions, and constraints (36)-(38) are relaxed by Lagrange multiplier λ^{c}_{j,i,t} for attaining lower-extremes of (39). The first and second terms in (39) define the total cost of P2P buying energy by j from i and the total revenue of P2P selling energy by i to j. In (39), the third term presents the product of Lagrange multiplier λ^{c}_{j,i,t} and the equilibrium quantity of P2P buying and selling energy, where the energy equilibrium constraint (38) corresponds to the Lagrange multiplier λ^{c}_{j,i,t} in (39)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"0 ≤Ppbj,i,t ≤Ppbj,t Cj,i,t; ∀(j, i) ∈J |j̸ = i, ∀t ∈T , (36) Ppsj,t 1 −Cj,i,t ≤Ppsj,i,t ≤0; ∀(j, i) ","equation_id":"(38)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Equation (38) refers to the energy matching constraint of prosumers' buying and selling in each P2P trade at time t, which implies that the amount of buying energy by prosumer j from prosumer i should be equal to the amount of selling energy by prosumer i to prosumer j at time t. P^{pb}_{j,i,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0, ∀(j,i) ∈ J | i ≠ j, ∀t∈T. (38)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"min Ppbj,i,t · pbj,t + Ppsi,j,t · psi,t Fig j∈J i∈J |i̸=j −λcj,i,t Ppbj,i,t + Ppsi,j,t τ; Ppsi,j,t ≤","equation_id":"(39)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To determine the individual P2P trading bids (P^{pb}_{j,i,t} and P^{ps}_{i,j,t}) and the P2P trading prices λ^{c}_{j,i,t} of prosumers (j and i), the optimal decision making problem is devised by the LMO that minimizes the mismatches between individual P2P trades as, min ∑_{j∈J} ∑_{i∈J | i≠j} ((P^{pb}_{j,i,t}·Λ^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t}·Λ^{ps}_{i,t}) − λ^{c}_{j,i,t}(P^{pb}_{j,i,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t})) τ; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0, ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, subject to: (36)−(38), (39) where Λ^{pb}_{j,t} and Λ^{ps}_{i,t} are the prices for P2P trading between prosumer j and prosumer i at time t."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":"1719","section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"0 ≤Ppbj,i,t ≤Ppbj,t Cj,i,t; ∀(j, i) ∈J |j̸ = i, ∀t ∈T , (36) Ppsj,t 1 −Cj,i,t ≤Ppsj,i,t ≤0; ∀(j, i) ","equation_id":"(38)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Equation (38) refers to the energy matching constraint of prosumers’ buying and selling in each P2P trade at time $t$, which implies that the amount of buying energy by prosumer $j$ from prosumer $i$ should be equal to the amount of selling energy by prosumer $i$ to prosumer $j$ at time $t$. $P_{j,i,t}^{pb} + P_{i,j,t}^{ps} = 0; P_{i,j,t}^{ps} \\le 0, \\forall (j,i) \\in J | i \\ne j, \\forall t \\in T. \\quad (38)$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e003","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"1719","section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"min Ppbj,i,t · pbj,t + Ppsi,j,t · psi,t Fig j∈J i∈J |i̸=j −λcj,i,t Ppbj,i,t + Ppsi,j,t τ; Ppsi,j,t ≤","equation_id":"(39)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To determine the individual P2P trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}$ and $P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and the P2P trading prices $\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$ of prosumers ($j$ and $i$), the optimal decision making problem is devised by the LMO that minimizes the mismatches between individual P2P trades as, $\\min \\sum_{j\\in J}\\sum_{i\\in J|i\\ne j} ((P_{j,i,t}^{pb}\\cdot \\Lambda_{j,t}^{pb}+P_{i,j,t}^{ps}\\cdot \\Lambda_{i,t}^{ps})-\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}(P_{j,i,t}^{pb}+P_{i,j,t}^{ps})\\tau);$ $P_{i,j,t}^{ps}\\le 0, \\forall (j,i)\\in J|j\\ne i, \\forall t\\in T,$ subject to: (36)-(38), (39)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e004","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"1719","section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"energy by i to j. In (39), the third term presents the product of Lagrange multiplier λcj,i,t and th","equation_id":"(39)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where $\\Lambda_{j,t}^{pb}$ and $\\Lambda_{i,t}^{ps}$ are the prices for P2P trading between prosumer $j$ and prosumer $i$ at time $t$. The objective function (39) yields P2P trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}$ and $P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and a P2P trading price $\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$ of the optimal solution using Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) conditions, and constraints (36)-(38) are relaxed by Lagrange multiplier $\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$ for attaining lower-extremes of (39). The first and second terms in (39) define the total cost of P2P buying energy by $j$ from $i$ and the total revenue of P2P selling energy by $i$ to $j$. In (39), the third term presents the product of Lagrange multiplier $\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$ and the equilibrium quantity of P2P buying and selling energy, where the energy equilibrium constraint (38) corresponds to the Lagrange multiplier $\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$ in (39)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-matching","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","quote":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E36","quote":"The objective function (39) yields P2P trading bids (P^{pb}_{j,i,t} and P^{ps}_{i,j,t}) and a P2P trading price λ^{c}_{j,i,t} of the optimal solution using Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) conditions, and constraints (36)-(38) are relaxed by Lagrange multiplier λ^{c}_{j,i,t} for attaining lower-extremes of (39)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E36","quote":"the energy equilibrium constraint (38) corresponds to the Lagrange multiplier λ^{c}_{j,i,t} in (39)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c0e2ed9629a7fd0e1b04bf3cf309367bd76ff3a9631fd5f732818d0fdc10fba7","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied source gives Eq. (39), the LMO local-clearing optimization for individual P2P quantities and P2P trading prices, and explicitly states that the P2P trading price λ^c_{j,i,t} is obtained from the optimal solution via KKT conditions and corresponds to the Lagrange multiplier of energy-equilibrium constraint (38). Eq. (39) and Eq. (38) are transcribed as source expressions. The source does not display the full KKT stationarity derivation, so no such stationarity equation is invented. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the declared clearing.local → pricing.local statement: the local clearing optimization determines bilateral quantities and yields P2P clearing prices, with the energy-equilibrium constraint corresponding to the price multiplier."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"Eq. (39) is the LMO clearing optimization. It determines bilateral quantities on the clearing side and the P2P trading price multiplier on the pricing side, so it binds both nodes and the declared clearing → pricing link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"Eq. (38) is the energy-equilibrium constraint that the source says corresponds to λ^c_{j,i,t} in (39); it links cleared bilateral quantities to the price multiplier and therefore to the pricing side of the declared edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Individual P2P buying quantity is an output of the local clearing optimization and is bounded by prosumer bids/status in (36); it is not itself the clearing → pricing edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-Pps-ijt","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Individual P2P selling quantity is an output of the local clearing optimization and is nonpositive; it is a clearing-side quantity, not the price edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"The source says (39) yields the P2P trading price λ^c_{j,i,t} and that it is the Lagrange multiplier of (38); this is exactly the price object of the declared clearing → pricing link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Λ^{pb}_{j,t} is a P2P trading price coefficient appearing in the buying term of (39); it is bound to the pricing node as a price input, not to a new edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-ps-it","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Λ^{ps}_{i,t} is a P2P trading price coefficient appearing in the selling term of (39); it is bound to the pricing node as a price input, not to a new edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-tau","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"τ multiplies the double-sum objective in (39), so it is a time-slot factor on the clearing optimization; it is not a price object and does not itself define an edge."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm the exact subscript order for P^{ps} in (37) versus (38)-(39): the supplied text uses P^{ps}_{j,i,t} in (37) and P^{ps}_{i,j,t} in (38)-(39), without an explicit cross-subscript definition.","Confirm whether λ^{c}_{j,i,t} is explicitly an optimization decision variable of (39) or only the KKT multiplier of constraint (38); the source says (39) yields the P2P trading price and also that (38) corresponds to this multiplier.","Confirm the placement and scope of τ in (39): the supplied transcription places τ after the summed parentheses, so it multiplies the whole double sum; the typeset PDF should verify this.","Confirm the units of λ^c and the Λ price terms: Fig. 12 reports prices in ¢ and amounts in kW, while the general network model uses p.u. for network variables."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
